<title>USA: June Brent slips in late U.S. paper trading.</title>
<headline>June Brent slips in late U.S. paper trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Sea Brent slipped in active late U.S. paper trading on Tuesday, traders said.</p>
<p>A full boat of June Brent traded at $18.08 a barrel, down four cents from the settlement of the International Petroleum Exchange (IPE) in London.</p>
<p>A series of June Brent partials changed hands at $18.05, $18.06, $18.07, $18.10 and $18.12.</p>
<p>May/June Brent traded twice at -20 cents and -22 cents a barrel.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
